at cannot have changed — cache the main-KV (ladder 1.0, 2026-08-20)\n230:### 2.6 A selection sort is not a top-k — single-CTA radix select (ladder 1.2, 2026-08-20)\n341:### 2.7 Change which kernel the bit-exactness claim is *against* — `index_score` as a register-tiled GEMM (ladder 1.5, 2026-08-20)\n413:### 2.8 The one adopted win that is not a kernel — actually serve the head you trained (ladder 2.2, 2026-08-20)\n440:### 2.9 `sparse_attn` — stage the gathered row in shared memory, and vectorise the load without losing bit-exactness (ladder 1.7, 2026-08-20)\n515:### 2.10 Join a side stream where the data is needed, not where it was forked (ladder 1.11, 2026-08-20)\n562:## 3. Precision and layout\n595:## 4. What every adopted change has in common","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
