{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CeF9Wj3HRZUxZRgYo3WPb","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01LspL1vGMbk45YV2qtesaHv","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/patrickd/deepseek-v4-flash-0731-cuda; cat > evidence/decode_loop/COMMIT_MSG_1p12.txt <<'MSGEOF'\n1.12: gemm_fp32 gets a (4x4) warp tile -- the ratio-128 emit spike falls 40.76 -> 14.50 ms (2.82x, populations disjoint) and the drift-free paired forward is -1.963 +/- 1.504 ms, band excluding zero, entirely in Term A\n\nWHAT WAS MEASURED\n\n`gemm_fp32`'s M=K path was one warp per (8-row chunk of A, one row of B), with the chunk loop on\nthe HOST. `compressor_emit_group` calls it at M = ratio = 128, N = d = 512, K = DIM = 4096 on the\ntwenty ratio-128 layers, so B = [512,4096] f32 = 8.39 MB was walked sixteen times, in sixteen\nseparate launches, twice per layer. A warp owning MM rows of A and NN rows of B issues MM+NN loads\nfor MM*NN*4 FMAs, so operand traffic is M*N*K*(1/NN + 1/MM): the shipped (8,1) is 1.125, (4,4) is\n0.375. The m-chunk loop also moves from the host to gridDim.y.\n\nSeventeen tiles benchmarked at the four shapes the engine issues (tools/f32mk_bench.cu), against\nthe EXACT pre-1.12 code as the baseline arm (DSV4_F32MK_TILE=8x0):\n\n  [128,512]x[512,4096]  strided emit, x40/step   0.5744 -> 0.2477 ms   2.32x\n  [8,1024]x[1024,4096]  indexer emit main, x42   0.0729 -> 0.0407 ms   1.79x\n  [8,256] x[256,4096]   indexer emit idx,  x42   0.0331 -> 0.0177 ms   1.87x\n  [5,64]  x[64,4096]    idx_weights_proj,  x21 on EVERY step   0.0143 -> 0.0144   1.00x\n\nThe last row is why the tile is OFF below M=8: at (4,4) that GEMV becomes a 4-row chunk plus a\n1-row tail and goes 0.0148 -> 0.0205 ms, and it fires 21x per forward against the emit shapes' once\nevery 4 or 128 positions. The guard also makes both A/B arms identical below M=8.\n\nIN THE ENGINE THE SAVING IS TWICE WHAT THE BENCH PREDICTED. The bench reuses one 8.39 MB B across\n200 reps, so 15 of its 16 passes are L2 hits on a 32 MB L2; the engine walks 20 layers x 2 matrices\n= 335 MB of distinct weights, so the passes removed are DRAM. Predicted -13.07 ms per emit step,\nmeasured -26.26. tools/emit_spike.py, pooled over four checkpoint loads:\n\n  cattn:compress, steps with a ratio-128 boundary  n=69   40.76 [39.92,45.22] -> 14.50 [14.29,14.64]\n                                                          -26.26 ms, 2.82x, populations DISJOINT\n  verify TOTAL excess on those steps               n=69   +63.17 -> +34.26   -28.91 ms\n  verify TOTAL excess on ratio-4 boundary steps    n=1811 +13.52 -> +11.03   -2.49 ms\n  cattn:q_proj excess on ratio-4 boundary steps    n=1811  +4.61 ->  +3.92   -0.69 ms\n\nThe ratio-4 row is what carries the throughput -- 62.8 % of steps have a ratio-4 boundary, and 1.8\nestablished that the side-stream emit's contention lands in cattn:q_proj. The item's own ranking\n(\"LOW on throughput\") was wrong about where the win would come from.\n\nWHAT IT MEANS\n\nDrift-free paired over 18 legs and FOUR checkpoint loads: -1.963 +/- 1.504 ms/forward, 14/18 legs\nfaster, 2 SE [-3.467, -0.459], band EXCLUDING zero. TERM A as pre-registered: flat -2.348 +/- 3.302\nagainst context +0.0533 +/- 0.4038 per 1000, R^2 0.004. So a 125.11 -> 123.15 ms (1.522x ->\n1.499x the 82.18 ms floor); b unchanged at 1.887.\n\nThe mark-level instrument predicts that band from a different measurement entirely:\n0.628 x 2.49 + 0.0239 x 26.42 = -2.20 ms/forward, which falls inside [-3.467, -0.459]. Two\ninstruments, one number.\n\nAND ONE ARM ORDER CALLED IT A NULL AGAIN. Control-first: -0.892, 2 SE [-2.134, +0.350], 10/18.\nChange-first: -3.033, 2 SE [-5.372, -0.695], 13/18. Pooled: -1.963, [-3.467, -0.459], 14/18, drift\n+1.071 +/- 1.115. Exactly 1.11's lesson (traps 33) on the very next item.\n\nBIT-EXACTNESS. gate_bf16w now sweeps all 18 dispatchable tiles INCLUDING the pre-1.12 8x0 arm, at 7\nvalues of M and 2 of N (N=254 is the guarded-store tail): 252 comparisons, worst max|diff| = 0.\nNegative control: perturb the epilogue by one part in 1e7 and 17 of 18 tiles FAIL while 8x0\ncorrectly does not. build/decode emitted identical generated ids in both arms with LOSSLESS PASS,\nand 11 in-situ gates pass in both arms. The sweep-level text-identity column is NOT usable under\nDSV4_DPROF and the null control proves it: two loads of the SAME binary also gave 0/18\nbyte-identical.\n\nTHE FIRST ENGINE A/B WAS A FALSE NULL AND COST FOUR LOADS. DSV4_F32MK_TILE=8x0 was rejected by its\nown parser (`nn > 0`), so both arms ran 4x4 and the mark moved -0.03 ms. The tell was that the null\nwas TOO CLEAN for a 3.5 %-spread instrument. The engine now prints `[f32mk] tile MMxNN` on the first\ngemm_fp32 of the process, the tile list is a whitelist rather than a parse, and the harness EXITS\nNON-ZERO if the two arms log the same tile. The wasted pair is kept as fit_1p12null_* because it is\nthis ladder's best null control (+0.512, 2 SE [-0.969, +1.993] on identical code, and the\nconditional mark reproducing to 0.03 ms).\n\nWHAT IT LEAVES. cattn:compress on an emit step is still 14.50 ms against a 335 MB / 1.40 ms byte\nfloor -- 4.3 % of roofline -- because at (4,4) the kernel is register- and issue-bound, not\ntraffic-bound: (6,6), (4,8) and (8,4) all measured SLOWER than (4,4). The next factor is tensor\ncores or a shared-memory B stage, and it is a new item.\n\nNEW FILES. tools/f32mk_bench.cu (bench AND gate, in build_gate.sh), tools/emit_spike.py\n(schedule-conditional mark distribution), scripts/f32mkn_ab_run.sh (9 phases, both arm orders,\nnamed in detach_audit.sh in this commit), DSV4_GEMM_TRACE=1 (per-(route,M,N,K) call-site histogram,\noff by default -- it is what proved the shape was reached and the arm was not).\n\nWIKI. kernel-optimisations.md 2.11 (the adoption) and 1.1 (all five \"read B once\" sites tiled M\nonly); measurement-and-traps.md 34 (the arm switch that never switched) and 35 (a byte-identity gate\nrun past the length at which the engine is not byte-identical); context-scaling.md (1.12 is the\nfirst clean \"no, it is not the context term\"); README.md state table.\nMSGEOF\nwc -l evidence/decode_loop/COMMIT_MSG_1p12.txt; head -1 evidence/decode_loop/COMMIT_MSG_1p12.txt","description":"Write the prepared commit message"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":708,"cache_read_input_tokens":271065,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":708},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"705b7178-c5fc-49bd-87a2-7fdc5167c57f","uuid":"6e77f94e-e398-4180-967d-f17bb8677ac4","timestamp":"2026-08-21T03:01:26.363Z","request_id":"req_011CeF9Whv4V4oRY5TwfhXdw"}
