{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CeF9Zq9yCNPwCXy4LwRdL","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Iteration 9 complete — ladder item **1.12** done, adopted default on.\n\n## What changed\n\n`gemm_fp32`'s M=K path was a **1-D tile**: one warp per (8-row chunk of A, one row of B), with the chunk loop on the *host*. `compressor_emit_group` calls it at M=128, N=512, K=4096 on the twenty ratio-128 layers, so B (8.39 MB f32) was walked 16 times in 16 separate launches, twice per layer.\n\nIt now gets a **(4,4) warp tile** with the m-loop in `gridDim.y`. Operand traffic goes `M·N·K·(1/1 + 1/8) → M·N·K·(1/4 + 1/4)`; 16 launches become 1.\n\n## What was measured\n\n| | before | after | |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `cattn:compress` on ratio-128 emit steps (n=69, 4 loads) | 40.76 [39.92, 45.22] | **14.50** [14.29, 14.64] | **−26.26 ms, 2.82×**, populations disjoint |\n| verify TOTAL excess on ratio-4 emit steps (n=1811, 62.8 % of steps) | +13.52 | **+11.03** | −2.49 ms |\n| drift-free paired forward, 18 legs × 4 loads | — | — | **−1.963 ± 1.504 ms, 14/18, band [−3.467, −0.459]** |\n\nTerm A as pre-registered (flat −2.348 ± 3.302 vs context +0.0533 ± 0.4038 per 1000, R² 0.004). **`a` 125.11 → 123.15 ms**; `b` unchanged. The mark-level prediction `0.628×2.49 + 0.0239×26.42 = −2.20` falls inside the throughput band — two instruments, one number.\n\nBit-exact: 252 tile×shape comparisons at `max|diff| = 0` with a live negative control (17 of 18 tiles fail when the epilogue is perturbed by 1e-7), identical generated ids, LOSSLESS PASS, 22 in-situ gate runs across both arms.\n\n## Two things worth flagging\n\n**The item's premise was wrong in three places** — `ntok` is `ratio`, not `2*ratio`; B is 8.39 MB, not 33.55; 16 passes, not 32. The mechanism survived; the arithmetic didn't.\n\n**The first engine A/B was a false null and cost four loads.** `DSV4_F32MK_TILE=8x0` was rejected by its own parser (`nn > 0`), so both arms ran 4×4 and the mark moved −0.03 ms. The tell was that the null was *too clean* for a 3.5 %-spread instrument. Fixed structurally: the engine prints the tile it resolved, the tile list is a whitelist, and the harness exits non-zero if both arms log the same one. The wasted pair is kept as this ladder's best null control.\n\nAnd again, as in 1.11: **one arm order alone called this a null** (−0.892, 2 SE [−2.134, +0.350]).\n\nWiki updated in the same iteration: `kernel-optimisations.md` §2.11 and §1.1, `measurement-and-traps.md` §34/§35, `context-scaling.md`, and the `README.md` state table.\n\nI could not commit or push — `.claude/settings.json` denies `git add/commit/push`. Per `scripts/decode_loop.sh:299`, the driver commits from a prepared message, so I wrote `evidence/decode_loop/COMMIT_MSG_1p12.txt` for it to pick up. Nothing is resident on the GPU and 107 GiB is free."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":579,"cache_read_input_tokens":275469,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":579},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"705b7178-c5fc-49bd-87a2-7fdc5167c57f","uuid":"5bf549c8-925a-4140-a0b8-ec6b3066313b","timestamp":"2026-08-21T03:01:55.869Z","request_id":"req_011CeF9ZoXzBpVuaBGAdLkcj"}
